eceived_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatkodima/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rails/rails/issues/comments/743434035","html_url":"https://github.com/rails/rails/issues/40804#issuecomment-743434035","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rails/rails/issues/40804","id":743434035,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDc0MzQzNDAzNQ==","user":{"login":"russellrichardson","id":152632,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MjYzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/152632?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/russellrichardson","html_url":"https://github.com/russellrichardson","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/russellrichardson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/russellrichardson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/russellrichardson/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/russellrichardson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/russellrichardson/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/russellrichardson/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/russellrichardson/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/russellrichardson/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/russellrichardson/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2020-12-11T21:23:33Z","updated_at":"2020-12-11T21:23:33Z","body":"I preferred to keep the keys matching the names of the IANA time zones. Makes for simpler code between a mobile app and a Rails API. I could change them to alpha-numeric or underscores but then I have to write code as a workaround to translate the IANA time zones in to the keys. Has anyone considered adding a `_methods: false` option for enums so these methods are not generated? That would solve my problem since I do not use them for this use case. Another option would be adding another option that allows you to customize the character replacement. e.g. \r\n\r\n```\r\n  enum timezone: {\r\n    'Etc/GMT+1' => 1,\r\n    'Etc/GMT-1' => 2\r\n   }, name_for_this: {\r\n     \"/\" => \"_\",\r\n     \"+\" => \"plus\",\r\n     \"-\" => \"minus\"\r\n   }\r\n```\r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rails/rails/issues/comments/743434035/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"russellrichardson","id":152632,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MjYzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/152632?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/russellrichardson","html_url":"https://github.com/russellrichardson","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/russellrichardson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/russellrichardson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/russellrichardson/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/russellrichardson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/russellrichardson/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/russellrichardson/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/russellrichardson/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/russellrichardson/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/russellrichardson/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rails/rails/issues/comments/743441498","html_url":"https://github.com/rails/rails/issues/40804#issuecomment-743441498","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rails/rails/issues/40804","id":743441498,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDc0MzQ0MTQ5OA==","user":{"login":"fatkodima","id":5657035,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2NTcwMzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5657035?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatkodima","html_url":"https://github.com/fatkodima","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatkodima/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatkodima/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatkodima/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatkodima/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatkodima/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatkodima/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatkodima/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatkodima/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatkodima/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2020-12-11T21:41:43Z","updated_at":"2020-12-11T21:41:43Z","body":"Seems like you are not using scopes too and probably really do not need an `enum`.\r\n\r\nHow about something like:\r\n```ruby\r\nclass Event < ApplicationRecord\r\n  TIMEZONES = {\r\n      'Etc/GMT+1' => 1,\r\n      'Etc/GMT-1' => 2\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  def timezone=(value)\r\n    self[:timezone] = TIMEZONES.fetch(value)\r\n  end\r\n\r\n  def timezone\r\n    TIMEZONES.key(self[:timezone])\r\n  end\r\nend\r\n```\r\n\r\nYou can expand on this, like maybe adding validations, etc.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rails/rails/issues/comments/743441498/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"fatkodima","id":5657035,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2NTcwMzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5657035?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatkodima","html_url":"https://github.com/fatkodima","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatkodima/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatkodima/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatkodima/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatkodima/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatkodima/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatkodima/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatkodima/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatkodima/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fatkodima/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rails/rails/issues/comments/743447165","html_url":"https://github.com/rails/rails/issues/40804#issuecomment-743447165","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rails/rails/issues/40804","id":743447165,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDc0MzQ0NzE2NQ==","user":{"login":"russellrichardson","id":152632,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MjYzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/152632?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/russellrichardson","html_url":"https://github.com/russellrichardson","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/russellrichardson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/russellrichardson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/russellrichardson/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/russellrichardson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/russellrichardson/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/russellrichardson/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/russellrichardson/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/russellrichardson/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/russellrichardson/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2020-12-11T21:55:06Z","updated_at":"2020-12-11T21:55:06Z","body":"I could do that, but to me that code is just reimplementing enum, especially if I start to add validations. I'd probably end up doing something like this : \r\n```ruby\r\n  enum timezone: {\r\n    'Etc_GMT_plus_1' => 1,\r\n    'Etc_GMT_minus_1' => 2\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  INVALID_TZ_FIX = {\r\n    \"Etc/GMT+1\" => \"Etc_GMT_plus_1\",\r\n    \"Etc/GMT-1\" => \"Etc_GMT_minus_1\"\r\n  }\r\n\r\n  def timezone=(value)\r\n    if INVALID_TZ_FIX.has_key?(value)\r\n      super(INVALID_TZ_FIX[value])\r\n    else\r\n      super(value)\r\n    end\r\n  end\r\n\r\n  def timezone\r\n    val = super\r\n    if INVALID_TZ_FIX.key(val)\r\n      INVALID_TZ_FIX.key(val)\r\n    else\r\n      val\r\n    end\r\n  end\r\n```","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rails/rails/issues/comments/743447165/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"russellrichardson","id":152632,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MjYzMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/152632?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/russellrichardson","html_url":"https://github.com/russellrichardson","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/russellrichardson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/russellrichardson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/russellrichardson/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/russellrichardson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/russellrichardson/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/russellrichardson/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/russellrichardson/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/russellrichardson/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/u